OL,3,GNEWSAMedic's memories 'vivid' after
OL,4,Atreating 9/11 victims
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Everything was very hushed. The dust
OL,7,Fhad the effect of deadening all sounds.
OL,8,FIt's like as if it was on a snowy day -
OL,9,Fyou could hear voices but they sounded
OL,10,Fdistant."
OL,12,FDoctor Sam Allen remembers the day of
OL,13,Fthe 9/11 attacks vividly. He was one of
OL,14,Fthe doctors who helped the wounded.
OL,16,FThat day, he was on board a plane that
OL,17,Fhad stopped to refuel at JFK Airport in
OL,18,FNew York when he witnessed the second
OL,19,Fplane hit the Twin Towers of the World
OL,20,FTrade Center.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,362,360,200,160,0,100
